-- title:
--   Realisation of the GL₂(ℚ_q)-span of an adelic lift
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $g$ a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(M)$, $q$ a prime, and $\Phi$ a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $g$, i.e. $\Phi$ is invariant under left multiplication by the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, invariant under right multiplication by the image under [`AdelicDock.finEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145) of the subgroup [`NumberField.AdelicLevel.finiteLevelOne`](def/NumberField_AdelicLevel.html#L418) attached to the ideal generated by $M$, and satisfies $\Phi(h) = (g \mid_2 \mathrm{ratArchGL2}(h))(i)$ for every $h$ whose finite part `glFin` is $1$ and whose real component `ratArchGL2` has positive determinant. Then there exist a type $V$ in `Type`, an additive commutative group and $\mathbb{C}$-module structure on it, a distributive action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ on $V$ commuting with the scalars, such that the submodule of vectors of $V$ fixed by every element of [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup q 1`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181) (the matrices $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ with all entries of $x - 1$ and of $x^{-1} - 1$ of norm $\le q^{-1}$) is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$, together with a $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $f$ from $V$ to [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ (the span of the adelic translates of $\Phi$) which is $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant, injective, and whose range is exactly the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the set of translates $x \cdot \Phi$, $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$.
--
--   This packages the span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-translates of an adelic lift of a weight-two cusp form as an abstract $\mathbb{C}$-representation of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ with finite-dimensional invariants under the congruence subgroup of level $q$, the shape required for the local theory of newvectors and conductors. It is used in the analysis of the local components of a newform, namely by [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_isCuspidalOfType_gl2ReductionRep_of_inertia_labels_eq_pow_of_irreducible_odd_of_cast_eq_neg_one`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_isCuspidalOfType_gl2ReductionRep_of_inertia_labels_eq_pow_of_irreducible_odd_of_cast_eq_neg_one).
